+      "problem": "The 'Disabled features are removed from the catalog' AC and spec section 2 (deployment gate) require the platform flag to gate the feature end-to-end, but _append_request_user_input_tool_if_enabled and the system-prompt injection key only on the per-assistant interactive_features config. The FE hides the form section behind the flag, yet a direct API POST setting interactive_features registers request_user_input on deployments where features:interactiveElements is off. Contrast: hedging checks customer_config.is_feature_enabled('requestHedging') in assistant_handlers.",
+      "impact": "Platform kill-switch is UI-only; the feature stays active on the backend when disabled.",
