+# EPMCDME-13259 — Interactive user input in CodeMie agent chat (Design Spec)
+
+**Date**: 2026-07-16 · **Status**: Approved by user (design walkthrough)
+**Repos**: `codemie` (backend) + `codemie-ui` (frontend), branch `feature/EPMCDME-13259-interactive-chat-input` in each
+**Complexity**: XXL 32/36, split-required overridden by user — single run
+**Architecture decision (user)**: extend the existing NDJSON protocol with A2UI-style fixed-schema payloads and own React components. No CopilotKit / AG-UI adoption.
+
+## Problem
+
+CodeMie agent chat is text-only. The agent cannot request explicit structured decisions (approve/reject), option selections, or validated form input; users can only reply free-text. The assistant configuration has no way to control which interactive capabilities an agent may use.
+
+## Key decisions (made during brainstorming)
+
+1. **Pause/resume: turn-based.** The agent "pauses" by ending its turn after emitting an interactive request; the user's structured response arrives as a normal chat request and is delivered to the rebuilt agent as the tool result. No server-side suspended runs, no checkpointer in the chat path. Survives pod restarts by construction.
+2. **Emission: dedicated tool `request_user_input`.** The tool's dynamically-built args schema IS the catalog; disabled features are physically absent from the schema (removed, not hidden).
+3. **State: derivation by `request_id`.** Messages are immutable; an element is "submitted" iff the history contains a response referencing its `request_id`.
+4. **Response UX: compact chip.** The structured response is persisted and rendered as a compact user message («✓ Approve», «✓ Selected: A, B»).
+
+## §1. Protocol (shared contract)
+
+New backend module `src/codemie/chains/interactive.py`, mirrored TS types in `src/types/entity/interactive.ts`.
+
+```python
+# Discriminated union by "type"
+Element = Column | Row | Text | Button | MultipleChoice | Dropdown | DatePicker | TextField | CheckBox
+
+class InteractiveRequest(BaseModel):
+    request_id: str            # uuid, assigned by backend
+    surface: list[Element]     # component tree
+
+class InteractiveResponse(BaseModel):
+    request_id: str
+    kind: Literal["action", "choice", "form", "text_fallback"]
+    payload: dict              # {"action": "approve"} | {"selected": [...]} | {"values": {...}} | {"text": "..."}
+```
+
+Element definitions (fixed schema v1):
+- Layout (always available when any feature enabled): `Column{children}`, `Row{children}`, `Text{content}`
+- `Button{id, label, style?}` — available when `action_buttons` OR `short_forms` enabled
+- `MultipleChoice{id, options[], maxAllowedSelections}` — `1` = single-select; feature `choice`
+- `Dropdown{id, label, options[], placeholder?, required?}` — single-select drop-down, value-based answer `{value}`; feature `choice`
+- `TextField{id, label, validation?: {required?, regex?, email?}}` — feature `short_forms`
+- `CheckBox{id, label, validation?: {required?}}` — feature `short_forms`
+- `DatePicker{id, label, min?, max?, required?}` — ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` value `{value}`, inclusive `min`/`max` range; feature `short_forms`
+
+Wire changes:
+- `StreamedGenerationResult` (`chains/base.py`): new **optional** field `interactive_request: InteractiveRequest | None`. Ordinary NDJSON chunk; old clients ignore it; text-only chat untouched.
+- Chat request model: new **optional** field `interactive_response: InteractiveResponse | None`, plus the normal `text` carrying the chip display text.
+
+## §2. Backend — tool and catalog
+
+- Built-in tool `request_user_input`, registered by the engine builder only when the assistant has ≥1 interactive feature enabled.
+- **Dynamic args schema** from `InteractiveFeaturesConfig`: disabled feature ⇒ its element types are absent from the tool's JSON schema. Dependency rule: `Button` present when `action_buttons OR short_forms`.
+- Tool execution: validate payload against the enabled-elements schema (invalid ⇒ tool error returned to the model for retry), assign `request_id`, emit the `interactive_request` chunk via the event adapter → `ThreadedGenerator`, then **end the agent turn**.
+- Catalog is additionally described in a system-prompt section (`assistant_agent.py`): when to use elements, only from the enabled list.
+- Config: pydantic sub-model `InteractiveFeaturesConfig {action_buttons: bool, choice: bool, short_forms: bool}` → JSONB column `interactive_features` on `assistants` + alembic migration + field on `AssistantRequest`. Template: `hedging_config` end-to-end precedent. All defaults **off**.
+- Deployment gate: `features:interactiveElements` component in `config/customer/customer-config.yaml` (+ Helm ConfigMap note).
+
+## §3. Backend — response intake and history
+
+- The user's response arrives as a normal chat request carrying `interactive_response`. Server validates: `request_id` exists in this conversation and is not yet answered (duplicate ⇒ error); form values are **re-validated server-side** (required/regex/email) — client validation is not trusted.
+- Persistence: `GeneratedMessage` gets optional `interactive_request`; the user message stores `interactive_response` + display text. No mutation of stored messages; submitted state is derived.
+- History materialization: `Conversation.to_chat_history()` replays only message text to the LLM, so the structured response is materialized as deterministic structured text inside the user message («display text + `[Structured response to interactive request <id>]` + JSON payload») — not as a synthetic tool-call/result pair. If the user replied with free text instead of using the element, the message goes through unchanged (`text_fallback`) — text-only behavior never regresses.
+
+## §4. Frontend — chat rendering
+
+- New family `src/components/InteractiveElements/`: recursive fixed-schema tree renderer + `Button`, `MultipleChoice`, `Dropdown` (form `Select`), `DatePicker` (form `DatePicker`), `TextField`, `CheckBox`, `Column`, `Row`, `Text`. Short forms validated client-side (required/regex/email + date format/range); invalid submit blocked client-side.
+- `ChatAiMessage` renders the block after the markdown body (pattern: `ChatAiAuthPrompt`). Block state:
+  - **submitted** — a response with this `request_id` exists in history ⇒ disabled + selection marks;
+  - **active** — last message, generation idle;
+  - **stale** — earlier in history, unanswered ⇒ disabled.
+- `chatGeneration` store (valtio, all API in store): handle `interactive_request` in `_handleChunk`; new action `submitInteractiveResponse(requestId, kind, payload, displayText)` sending a normal chat request through the existing generation flow.
+- `ChatPrompt` free-text input is **not blocked** while an element is active (text fallback, §3).
+- Compact chip rendering for the structured user response in the history feed.
+
+## §5. Frontend — assistant form
+
+New accordion section **“Interactive features”** in `AssistantForm` (template: `HedgingConfig`): three toggles (Action buttons / Choices / Short forms). Section visibility behind `useFeatureFlag('interactiveElements')`. Wiring: Yup schema, `compareFormData.ts`, entity type in `assistant.ts`, mock-server `db.json` flag entry. Defaults: all off.
+
+## §6. Testing
+
+- **Backend (pytest)**: dynamic tool schema per config combination (incl. Button dependency rule); payload validation; chunk emission + turn end; `interactive_response` intake incl. duplicate answer rejection and server-side re-validation; history materialization of request/response pairs and `text_fallback`; migration.
+- **Frontend (vitest)**: unit — each element component + form validation; store — chunk handling, `submitInteractiveResponse`, state derivation; integration — AssistantForm section (create/edit), `ChatAiMessage` in submitted/active/stale states.
+
+## Acceptance criteria mapping
+
+| Ticket AC | Covered by |
+|---|---|
+| Chat UI displays interactive elements | §1, §4 |
+| Actions (Approve/Reject/…) delivered structured, agent continues | §1–§4 (turn-based) |
+| MultipleChoice single/multi via `maxAllowedSelections` | §1, §4 |
+| Short form submit, structured return | §1, §3, §4 |
+| Validation required/regex/email, invalid blocked | §4 (client) + §3 (server re-check) |
+| Agent pauses until explicit input, resumes after | §2–§3 (turn-based semantics) |
+| Element state updates without breaking chat context | §3–§4 (derivation by `request_id`) |
+| “Interactive features” block in assistant create/edit | §5 |
+| Disabled features removed from agent-exposed catalog | §2 (dynamic tool schema + prompt) |
+| Text-only chat not regressed | §1 (optional fields), §3 (`text_fallback`), §4 (prompt not blocked) |
